abstract: Initial AI transcription of the 1868 witness 奇症略述 (printed 奇症畧述), Bodleian
  Sinica2021. It contains 399 original-print units and 6538 Unicode code points from
  31 target physical faces in 19 official frames, with 32 located reading uncertainties.
  A separately disclosed inspected p12 edge fragment has unknown attribution and extent;
  no text or missing-character count is inferred. The preface date is distinct from
  the edition year. Seven uncertainty-ID aliases are metadata adaptations only. Independent
  reading is not applied; no human double collation, expert review, peer review or
  measured accuracy is claimed. Historical-document digitization only, without biological
  research or modern procedural interpretation.
